    {
      "claim": "The systematic and widespread nature of the attacks, coupled with the expressed aim of creating an ethnically homogeneous Serb state, demonstrates the specific intent (dolus specialis) required to constitute genocide.",
      "reasoning": "Genocide requires that the prohibited acts be committed \"with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group, as such\" (Genocide Convention, Art.2). The pattern of attacks across multiple regions, the targeting of civilian populations, and the documented objective of the Serb leadership to expel Croats indicate a coordinated policy aimed at destroying the Croat group, at least in part. Such circumstantial evidence is sufficient to infer the requisite specific intent under established international jurisprudence.",
