      "claim": "Even if intent to destroy the entire Croat population is not established, the intent to destroy a substantial part of that population—specifically the Croats residing in the six regions targeted by the attacks—fulfills the \"in whole or in part\" requirement of the Genocide Convention.",
      "reasoning": "The Convention’s definition expressly includes destruction \"in whole or in part\". The six regions affected comprised between 1.7 and 1.8 million Croats, roughly half of Croatia’s Croat population, representing a substantial part of the group. The deliberate targeting of these regions demonstrates an intent to eliminate that significant portion, thereby meeting the statutory threshold.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "genocide",
          "article": "2",
          "quoted_text": "any of the following acts committed with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group, as such"
